    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#h1",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "heading",
      "content": "INTRODUCTION"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s1",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "High-performance computing (HPC) is a cornerstone of computational fluid dynamics, enabling an ever-growing resolution i"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s2",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "Driven by hardware advances such as general-purpose processor (CPU) and accelerator-based (GPU) nodes, CFD software is r"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s3",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "The trend comes at an added software-complexity cost, and CFD developers now heavily rely on HPC libraries to offload co"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s4",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "In this direction, we present performance-oriented developments and the first parallel scalability results of WaterLily."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s5",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "Written in pure Julia, WaterLily is designed to be a compact and minimalist finite-volume incompressible-flow solver tha"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s6",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "This feature is enabled by separating computing workloads (typically for loops) from the algorithmic space-time discreti"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s7",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "By using Julia's metaprogramming support, the solver ultimately specialises each kernel to the available computing backe"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#h2",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "heading",
      "content": "MPI PARALLELISATION AND SCALING"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s8",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "Further leveraging Julia's scientific computing ecosystem, distributed-memory parallelism has been recently integrated i"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s9",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "Backed by the MPI.jl wrapper, IGG uses a Cartesian MPI communicator naturally mapping to regular grids, and offering CUD"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s10",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "Additionally, IGG works with different grid sizes, thus enabling halo updates within geometric-multigrid (GMG) levels wi"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#f1",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "figure",
      "content": "\\begin{figure}\n\\includegraphics[width=7.93cm]{./img/strong_scaling.pdf}\n\\includegraphics[width=7.93cm]{./img/weak_scalin"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s11",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "Strong and weak scalability results are presented in Figure \\ref{fig:scalability}."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s12",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "The tests are conducted with the SIMD single-thread CPU backend with single precision (FP32) and half-node occupancy (64"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s13",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "The test cases comprise a Taylor--Green vortex (TGV) at $Re=1600$ in a triple-periodic cubic domain, and flow past a sph"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s14",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "The MPI domain decomposition always minimizes the halo surface for a given number of processes."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s15",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "The strong-scalability results closely follow the ideal linear reduction in time per time-step, even super-linearly for "
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s16",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "The trend deteriorates when MPI halo updates dominate the local workload, once the smallest local subdomain dimension ap"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s17",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "The weak-scalability results maintain an efficiency $(E)$ above 90\\% for the small ($64^3$ cells) and large ($128^3$ cel"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s18",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "Beyond, efficiency drops due to intra-node memory-concurrency contention, motivating the 50\\% node occupancy."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s19",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "This reflects the memory-bound nature of the solver's stencil kernels \\cite{Williams2009}."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s20",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "While memory bandwidth is not saturated (checked with hardware counters), ranks compete to access the per-chiplet link t"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s21",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "Ranks are hence pinned with a uniform stride across the node."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s22",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "Beyond the node, weak scaling is nearly ideal, remaining above 96\\% up to 512 ranks and $10^9$ cells (Figure \\ref{fig:sc"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#h3",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "heading",
      "content": "ANISOTROPIC GEOMETRIC MULTIGRID SOLVER WITH ADAPTIVE UNDER-RELAXED RED-BLACK GAUSS--SEIDEL SMOOTHER"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s23",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "WaterLily's general-purpose Poisson solver is Preconditioned Conjugate Gradient (PCG), which applies to arbitrary grid s"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s24",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "However, its global inner products require costly reductions in MPI simulations, and the number of iterations increases "
    },
    {
      "element_id": "2607-07687#s25",
      "arxiv_id": "2607.07687",
      "kind": "sentence",
      "content": "For this reason, the default WaterLily solver uses GMG, which accelerates convergence by combining smoothers to remove h"
    }
